Id: root004w
Severity: WARN
Category: accounts
Check: check_root
Controls: CIS 5.4; NIST AC-6, AC-17; ISO 8.2, 8.5; CE User access control

The graphical login manager, xdm or an old gdm, is configured to let
root log in at the console (allowRootLogin, AllowRoot or
AllowRemoteRoot set to true). A graphical session runs far more code
as root than a shell does, and every bit of it is trusted with the
machine. Turn the setting off and log in as an ordinary user, using su
or sudo for the few things that need root.
